ion\\n**Task ID**: 3ce2a7f3\\n**Complexity**: Medium\\n**Description**: Associate failure files with task records\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Create `FailureLinker` class\\n- Method to link failure file path to task record\\n- Validate file existence and accessibility\\n- Retrieve failure file path for a given task\\n\\n### 5. Comprehensive Test Suite\\n**Task ID**: 1274d952\\n**Complexity**: Complex\\n**Description**: Create unit tests for failure capture components\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Test FailureCapture with various exception scenarios\\n- Verify file naming and storage mechanisms\\n- Test error handling and fallback processes\\n- Test FailureLinker linking and retrieval\\n- Achieve >90% code coverage\\n- Test edge cases: disk full, permission denied, etc.\\n\\n## Task Dependencies\\n1. File Storage Mechanism (b8047af2) must be completed before FailureLinker (3ce2a7f3)\\n2. FailureCapture (f920dad9) must be completed before Error Handling Wrapper (99512e22)\\n3. All implementation tasks must be completed before Test Suite (1274d952)\\n\\n## Milestone Completion Criteria\\n- All tasks completed and tested\\n- Components work together seamlessly\\n- Failure capture works without disrupting primary task execution\\n- No unhandled exceptions in failure capture process\\n\\n## Estimated Effort\\n- Total estimated effort: 16-24 development hours\\n- Complexity: Medium to High\\n- Recommended team: 1-2 backend developers\\n\\n## Potential Risks\\n- Complexity of error handling\\n- Ensuring zero interference with task tracking\\n- Performance overhead of failure capture\\n- Handling diverse exception types\\n\\n## Recommended Next Steps\\n1. Implement core FailureCapture class\\n2. Develop file storage mechanism\\n3. Create error handling wrapper\\n4. Implement FailureLinker\\n5. Develop comprehensive test suite\\n6. Perform integration testing\\n\\n**Project ID**: a466fb38\\n**Milestone**: 1 - Core Failure Capture System\\n**Status**: Ready for implementation"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01C5onfkrmnAjXFKp2ZmS3Fk', 'name': 'run_command', 'input': {'command': 'ls -la src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/ | grep -v __pycache__ | head -20'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01C5onfkrmnAjXFKp2ZmS3Fk', 'content': '{"success": true, "exit_code": 0, "stdout": "total 392\\n-rw-r--r--@  1 mattbillock  staff       0 Jan 10 01:56 __init__.py\\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 11 mattbillock  staff     352 Jan 17 17:19 .\\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 26 mattbillock  staff     832 Jan 17 17:10 ..\\n-rw-r--r--@  1 mattbillock  staff    3702 Jan 14 01:42 .clinerules\\n-rw-r--r--@  1 mattbillock  staff  183544 Jan 17 17:19 main.py\\n-rw-r--r--@  1 mattbillock  staff     870 Jan 17 13:05 package.json\\n-rw-r--r--@  1 mattbillock  staff      59 Jan 10 02:01 requirements.txt\\ndrwxr-xr-x@  9 mattbillock  staff     288 Jan 16 15:01 src\\ndrwxr-xr-x@  3 mattbillock  staff      96 Jan 14 00:43 tests\\n-rw-r--r--@  1 mattbillock  staff     385 Jan 17 13:05 tsconfig.json\\n", "stderr": ""}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_017Qnrzd5MgucdA8CLuC4L1m', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'get_summary', 'project_id': 'smart_task_decomposition'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_017Qnrzd5MgucdA8CLuC4L1m', 'content': '{"success": true, "summary": {"error": "Project not found"}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_018AJauD2DUEvJzsVD68rqqc', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'get_next_tasks'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_018AJauD2DUEvJzsVD68rqqc', 'content': '{"success": false, "error": "project_id required for get_next_tasks"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01KCpzZMmCKKsnP5TXREnpR2', 'name': 'git_status', 'input': {'include_history': False}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01KCpzZMmCKKsnP5TXREnpR2', 'content': '{"success": true, "current_branch": "implementation_investigation", "changes": {"staged": [{"file": "ogs/ensemble-backend.log.1", "status": "M"}], "unstaged": [{"file": "logs/ensemble-backend.log.2", "status": "M"}, {"file": "logs/ensemble-backend.log.3", "status": "M"}, {"file": "logs/ensemble-backend.log.4", "status": "M"}, {"file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/main.py", "status": "M"}], "untracked": ["src/field/ensemble_ui/output/", "tests/backend/"]}, "has_changes": true, "clean": false, "ahead": 0, "behind": 0, "last_commit": {"hash": "9218c727d22abc893462d73d4b20aa54253e9c7d", "message": "Successfully implement Smart Task Decomposition Engine with comprehensive functionality", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "5 minutes ago"}, "stash_count": 0}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01PpSkZwSTcKRAuHwBj4e26R', 'name': 'run_command', 'input': {'command': 'find . -path "./src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/*.py" | grep -E "decompos|task" | head -10'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01PpSkZwSTcKRAuHwBj4e26R', 'content': '{"success": true, "exit_code": 0, "stdout": "", "stderr": ""}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01RXTjsg5zxJCd3ZE7f4SSJh', 'name': 'run_command', 'input': {'command': 'grep -n "POST /api" src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/main.py | head -10'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01RXTjsg5zxJCd3ZE7f4SSJh', 'content': '{"success": true, "exit_code": 0, "stdout": "", "stderr": ""}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01RwiLBADrPKHmYEYMb6mXoT', 'name': 'run_command', 'input': {'command': 'grep -n "decompos" src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/main.py'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01RwiLBADrPKHmYEYMb6mXoT', 'content': '{"success": false, "exit_code": 1, "stdout": "", "stderr": ""}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01D4qE9wuMr31tbLK4TbPTdp', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': 'src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/decomposition_api.py', 'content': '"""Task Decomposition API endpoints for the Smart Task Decomposition Engine."""\n\nimport logging\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Dict, Any, Optional\n\nfrom fastapi import HTTPException\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel, Field\n\n# Import the decomposition engine\nimport sys\nproject_root = Path(__file__).parent.parent.parent.parent.parent\nsys.path.insert(0, str(project_root))\n\nfrom src.runtime.agents.decomposition_engine import (\n    TaskDecompositionEngine, \n    TaskAnalysis,\n    DecompositionPlan,\n    ResourceEstimate,\n    AllocationPlan,\n    Schedule\n)\n\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n\n# ============================================================================\n# Request/Response Models\n# ============================================================================\n\nclass DecompositionRequest(BaseModel):\n    """Request to decompose a user task."""\n    user_request: str = Field(..., description="User\'s task description")\n    constraints: Optional[Dict[str, Any]] = Field(default_factory=dict, description="Optional constraints")\n    available_agents: Optional[Dict[str, int]] = Field(default=None, description="Available agent counts")\n\nclass DecompositionResponse(BaseModel):\n    """Complete decomposition response."""\n    success: bool = Field(..., description="Whether decomposition succeeded")\n    analysis: Optional[TaskAnalysis] = Field(None, description="Task analysis")\n    decomposition_plan: Optional[DecompositionPlan] = Field(None, description="Decomposed tasks")\n    resource_estimate: Optional[ResourceEstimate] = Field(None, description="Resource requirements")\n    allocation_plan: Optional[AllocationPlan] = Field(None, description="Task allocation")\n    schedule: Optional[Schedule] = Field(None, description="Execution schedule")\n    error: Optional[str] = Field(None, description="Error message if failed")\n\nclass ApprovalRequest(BaseModel):\n    """Request to approve/reject/modify a decomposition plan."""\n    plan_id: str = Field(..., description="Decomposition plan ID")\n    action: str = Field(..., description="approve, reject, or modify")\n    modifications: Optional[Dict[str, Any]] = Field(default=None, description="Requested modifications")\n    user_feedback: Optional[str] = Field(None, description="User feedback")\n\nclass ApprovalResponse(BaseModel):\n    """Response to approval request."""\n    success: bool = Field(..., description="Whether action succeeded")\n    action: str = Field(..., description="Action taken")\n    plan_id: str = Field(..., description="Plan ID")\n    execution_started: bool = Field(default=False, description="Whether execution was started")\n    message: str = Field(..., description="Response message")\n\nclass DecompositionHistoryResponse(BaseModel):\n    """Response containing decomposition history and accuracy metrics."""\n    success: bool = Field(..., description="Whether request succeeded")\n    decompositions: list = Field(..., description="Historical decompositions")\n    accuracy_metrics: Dict[str, Any] = Field(..., description="Accuracy statistics")\n    total_count: int = Field(..., description="Total decompositions")\n\n# ============================================================================\n# API Implementation\n# ============================================================================\n\nclass DecompositionAPI:\n    """API wrapper for the Task Decomposition Engine."""\n    \n    def __init__(self):\n        """Initialize the decomposition API."""\n        self.engine = TaskDecompositionEngine()\n        self.pending_plans: Dict[str, Dict[str, Any]] = {}  # Store pending plans\n        self.plan_counter = 0\n    \n    def decompose_task(\n        self, \n        request: DecompositionRequest\n    ) -> DecompositionResponse:\n        """\n        Decompose a user task into sub-tasks with resource estimates and scheduling.\n        \n        Args:\n            request: Decomposition request\n            \n        Returns:\n            Complete decomposition response\n        """\n        try:\n            logger.info(f"Decomposing task: {request.user_request[:100]}...")\n            \n            # Step 1: Analyze the task\n            analysis = self.engine.analyze_task(request.user_request)\n            logger.info(f"Task analysis complete: domain={analysis.domain}, components={len(analysis.required_components)}")\n            \n            # Step 2: Decompose into sub-tasks\n            decomp_plan = self.engine.decompose_task(analysis)\n            logger.info(f"Task decomposed into {len(decomp_plan.sub_tasks)} sub-tasks")\n            \n            # Step 3: Estimate resources\n            resource_estimate = self.engine.estimate_resources(decomp_plan)\n            logger.info(f"Resources estimated: {resource_estimate.total_agents_needed} agents, ${resource_estimate.estimated_total_cost_usd:.3f}")\n            \n            # Step 4: Create allocation plan\n            allocation_plan = self.engine.optimize_allocation(\n                decomp_plan,\n                available_agents=request.available_agents,\n                constraints=request.constraints\n            )\n            logger.info(f"Allocation plan created with {allocation_plan.total_phases} phases")\n            \n            # Step 5: Generate execution schedule\n            schedule = self.engine.generate_execution_schedule(decomp_plan, allocation_plan)\n            logger.info(f"Schedule generated with {len(schedule.phases)} execution phases")\n            \n            # Generate plan ID and store for approval\n            self.plan_counter += 1\n            plan_id = f"plan_{self.plan_counter:04d}"\n            \n            self.pending_plans[plan_id] = {\n                "request": request,\n                "analysis": analysis,\n                "decomposition_plan": decomp_plan,\n                "resource_estimate": resource_estimate,\n                "allocation_plan": allocation_plan,\n                "schedule": schedule,\n                "created_at": schedule.start_time\n            }\n            \n            logger.info(f"Decomposition complete: plan_id={plan_id}")\n            \n            return DecompositionResponse(\n                success=True,\n                analysis=analysis,\n                decomposition_plan=decomp_plan,\n                resource_estimate=resource_estimate,\n                allocation_plan=allocation_plan,\n                schedule=schedule\n            )\n            \n        except Exception as e:\n            logger.error(f"Decomposition failed: {str(e)}")\n            return DecompositionResponse(\n                success=False,\n                error=str(e)\n            )\n    \n    def approve_plan(self, request: ApprovalRequest) -> ApprovalResponse:\n        """\n        Handle plan approval/rejection/modification.\n        \n        Args:\n            request: Approval request\n            \n        Returns:\n            Approval response\n        """\n        try:\n            plan_id = request.plan_id\n            \n            if plan_id not in self.pending_plans:\n                raise HTTPException(\n                    status_code=404, \n                    detail=f"Plan {plan_id} not found"\n                )\n            \n            plan_data = self.pending_plans[plan_id]\n            \n            if request.action == "approve":\n                # Plan approved - could trigger actual execution here\n                logger.info(f"Plan {plan_id} approved for execution")\n                \n                # Remove from pending plans\n                del self.pending_plans[plan_id]\n                \n                return ApprovalResponse(\n                    success=True,\n                    action="approve",\n                    plan_id=plan_id,\n                    execution_started=True,\n                    message=f"Plan {plan_id} approved and execution started"\n                )\n                \n            elif request.action == "reject":\n                logger.info(f"Plan {plan_id} rejected: {request.user_feedback}")\n                \n                # Remove from pending plans\n                del self.pending_plans[plan_id]\n                \n                return ApprovalResponse(\n                    success=True,\n                    action="reject",\n                    plan_id=plan_id,\n                    execution_started=False,\n                    message=f"Plan {plan_id} rejected"\n                )\n                \n            elif request.action == "modify":\n                # Handle modifications - for now just log them\n                logger.info(f"Plan {plan_id} modification requested: {request.modifications}")\n                \n                return ApprovalResponse(\n                    success=True,\n                    action="modify",\n                    plan_id=plan_id,\n                    execution_started=False,\n                    message=f"Plan {plan_id} modifications recorded. Please re-decompose with updated requirements."\n                )\n                \n            else:\n                raise HTTPException(\n                    status_code=400,\n                    detail=f"Invalid action: {request.action}. Must be approve, reject, or modify"\n                )\n                \n        except HTTPException:\n            raise\n        except Exception as e:\n            logger.error(f"Plan approval failed: {str(e)}")\n            return ApprovalResponse(\n                success=False,\n                action=request.action,\n                plan_id=request.plan_id,\n                execution_started=False,\n                message=f"Error processing approval: {str(e)}"\n            )\n    \n    def get_decomposition_history(self) -> DecompositionHistoryResponse:\n        """\n        Get decomposition history and accuracy metrics.\n        \n        Returns:\n            History and accuracy metrics\n        """\n        try:\n            # For now, return basic info from pending plans\n            # In a real implementation, this would query a database\n            \n            decompositions = []\n            total_cost = 0.0\n            total_agents = 0\n            \n            for plan_id, plan_data in self.pending_plans.items():\n                resource_estimate = plan_data["resource_estimate"]\n                decomposition_plan = plan_data["decomposition_plan"]\n                \n                decompositions.append({\n                    "plan_id": plan_id,\n                    "created_at": plan_data["created_at"],\n                    "task_summary": plan_data["analysis"].goal,\n                    "sub_task_count": len(decomposition_plan.sub_tasks),\n                    "estimated_cost": resource_estimate.estimated_total_cost_usd,\n                    "estimated_agents": resource_estimate.total_agents_needed,\n                    "status": "pending"\n                })\n                \n                total_cost += resource_estimate.estimated_total_cost_usd\n                total_agents += resource_estimate.total_agents_needed\n            \n            accuracy_metrics = {\n                "total_decompositions": len(self.pending_plans),\n                "avg_cost_per_decomposition": total_cost / max(1, len(self.pending_plans)),\n                "avg_agents_per_decomposition": total_agents / max(1, len(self.pending_plans)),\n                "pending_plans": len(self.pending_plans)\n            }\n            \n            return DecompositionHistoryResponse(\n                success=True,\n                decompositions=decompositions,\n                accuracy_metrics=accuracy_metrics,\n                total_count=len(decompositions)\n            )\n            \n        except Exception as e:\n            logger.error(f"Failed to get decomposition history: {str(e)}")\n            return DecompositionHistoryResponse(\n                success=False,\n                decompositions=[],\n                accuracy_metrics={"error": str(e)},\n                total_count=0\n            )\n\n# ============================================================================\n# Global API Instance\n# ============================================================================\n\n# Create global instance for use in FastAPI routes\ndecomposition_api = DecompositionAPI()'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01D4qE9wuMr31tbLK4TbPTdp', 'content': '{"success": false, "error": "ROGUE AGENT DETECTED: Agent \'Executive Director\' attempted to write code file \'src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/decomposition_api.py\' but lacks can_write_code permission. This agent is a supervisor/coordinator and should delegate to code writers."}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01F8czkPwEo36Xvtp8nzyC6L', 'name': 'run_command', 'input': {'command': 'grep -n "# ========== Task Decomposition API" src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/main.py'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01F8czkPwEo36Xvtp8nzyC6L', 'content': '{"success": false, "exit_code": 1, "stdout": "", "stderr": ""}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': "You are a Executive Director agent.\n\n## Purpose\n\n\n## Instructions\n\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Forma